> Note: There are additional images in the source link. There is no US units conversion on the source site.

Preheat oven to 200°C fan / 220°C / 425°F / Gas mark 7.

If you have not bought @lamb{850%g} (diced lamb), cut your lamb shoulder or leg into large chunks and place to one side.

Make oil marinade - Mix @olive oil{80%ml} in a bowl with @garlic puree{1%tbsp}, @sundried tomato puree{1%tbsp}, @black pepper{}, and @salt{}.

Add @potatoes{600%g} and all the vegetables: @courgette{1}(chopped chunky), @carrot{1%large}(chopped), @pepper{1}(green chopped chunky), @aubergine{1%small}(chopped chunky), @onion{1%large}(chopped) into a large #casserole dish{}.

Place @lamb{} on top of the vegetables, pour the marinade and @white wine{250%ml} over the top.

Add @thyme{}, @rosemary{}, and @sage{}, trying to keep the herbs on top so you can easily remove the herb stalks once cooked.

Place lid on the casserole dish and cook for ~{90%minutes}. If you do not have a lid, cover very well with kitchen foil.

Take the lid off, remove any thick herb stems. Stir in @olive oil{2%tbsp}. Cook for a further ~{20-30%minutes}.

Serve with fresh homemade bread to dip into the juices.
